      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "717f644d-bc73-502f-8f57-c402b48dc429",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Teams: Miami Dolphins, Kansas City Chiefs, New York Jets, Denver Broncos\n- People: Andy Reid, John Dorsey\n- Seasons: 2016 Miami Dolphins season, 2016 Kansas City Chiefs season\n- Roles: head coach, general manager\n- Events: Week 15 win, playoff berth, firing\n\nFacts:\n- The 2016 Kansas City Chiefs season was the franchise's 47th season in the National Football League and 57th overall.\n- The 2016 season was Andy Reid's fourth season as head coach of the Kansas City Chiefs.\n- The 2016 season was John Dorsey's fourth and final season as general manager of the Kansas City Chiefs.\n- In Week 15 of the 2016 season, the Miami Dolphins defeated the New York Jets and clinched their first winning record since 2008.\n- The following week, the Miami Dolphins clinched a playoff berth after the Kansas City Chiefs defeated the Denver Broncos.\n- John Dorsey was fired by the Kansas City Chiefs on June 22, 2017.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
